// PIN: a module declares each tor once across facet companions too —
// 140_024 covers the part boundary, 210_262 the same file. A `.kz`/`.kjs`
// facet pair repeating a name silently shadowed (registry dedup), and with
// matching signatures emitted two `greet_event` structs — a Zig duplicate-
// member error no caret could map back. KORU111 does not cover it: no `.k`
// contract exists. The caret lands on the redeclaring companion decl.

~import std/io
~import app/helper

~app/helper:greet(name: "World"): g |> std/io:print.ln("{{ g:s }}")
